DESCRIPTION Grounding band, a yes or no health question about every node; the answer names only nodes that exist and counts them right.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Are all the cluster nodes healthy right now?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "node")

# Deterministic guards on the failure of 2026-11-22 (conversation c6ce88c0): a node list too
# large for the agents' windows reached the table unread, three agents agreed on it, and the
# synthesis wrote "All 15 nodes" for a cluster of 14 and invented crew-node-01 to crew-node-10.
# Real nodes are named homelab-k8s-*; no node of this cluster is named crew-node-*. A cluster
# that really grows to 15 nodes makes the count guards stale, so move them with the cluster.
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "crew-node")
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "15 nodes")
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "additional nodes")

# Reference-grounded quality, deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew): the live node list is
# the ground truth, so a name the cluster does not have or a wrong count fails the answer whatever
# else it gets right.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The cluster has 14 nodes, all Ready with no pressure condition, so the answer is yes, they are healthy. A correct answer gives the count the Kubernetes API reports and names only nodes that exist (all named homelab-k8s-...; for example the control-plane nodes homelab-k8s-1-cp, -cp-2 and -cp-3). Any node name that is not in the cluster (a name such as crew-node-01), any count other than the live count, or any claim about nodes that were never listed is fabrication and fails the answer. If a node is NotReady or under pressure, a correct answer says which node (the count and the state may drift; the constant is that every name and number matches the live node list, never invented).")
